<p>She can also get as hot as some of the lowest temperatures you would find inside of a nuclear reactor. That was the baseline I used to decide how hot she should be. I chose 400 degrees because I felt like anything hotter was stretching it, not to mention made containment an issue since she could melt lead at that point.</p>
